.\" Title: vrw-freeze
.\" Author: vrw contributors
.\" Manual section: 1
.\" Process this file with
.\"   groff -man -Tascii vrw-freeze.1

.TH VRW\-FREEZE 1 "2025" "vrw" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
vrw\-freeze \- suspend a running command via SIGSTOP

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vrw
\fBfreeze\fR [\fIPID\fR] [\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Freeze (suspend) a running command by sending it SIGSTOP. The command's OS process is paused but not terminated; all its state is preserved in memory. Use \fBvrw thaw\fR to resume execution from where it was suspended.

This is the CLI equivalent of \fBPOST /api/commands/:id/freeze\fR. The subcommand first discovers a running vrw instance (using \fB\-\-target PID\fR if specified, or auto-selecting if only one exists), then resolves the given OS PID to a command UUID via the instance's API, and sends the freeze request.

Freezing is useful for temporarily suspending resource-intensive tasks (compilations, data processing) without losing their progress. The frozen command remains visible in the web UI and CLI listings with its state unchanged. While frozen, the command does not consume CPU time but its memory remains allocated.

.SH ARGUMENTS

.TP
.B PID
OS process ID of the command to freeze. This is the child process PID (shown in \fBvrw list\fR output), not the vrw instance PID. When \fB\-\-interactive\fR is used, this argument can be omitted.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Present a numbered list of running commands and let the user select
which ones to freeze by typing space-separated numbers (e.g. "1 3 5").
Requires a terminal (stdin must be a TTY).

.SH EXAMPLES

.PP
Freeze a running command:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrw list\fR
INSTANCE  PID: 12345  PORT: 9090  BIND: 127.0.0.1  DAEMON: no  DISPLAY: yes
  5678       cargo build                           CERT: -

\fB$ vrw freeze 5678\fR
Command with PID 5678 frozen (SIGSTOP) on instance 12345
.fi
.RE

.PP
Resume a frozen command:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrw thaw 5678\fR
Command with PID 5678 thawed (SIGCONT) on instance 12345
.fi
.RE

.PP
Equivalent curl:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB# Resolve PID to command ID first, then freeze:\fR
curl -s -X POST "http://localhost:9090/api/commands/abc123/freeze" \e
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \e
  -d '{}'
.fi
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
.B 0
Command frozen successfully.

.TP
.B 1
Error (no running instances, PID not found, connection refused, etc.).

.SH SEE ALSO

.BR vrw (1),
.BR vrw\-thaw (1),
.BR vrw\-stop\-command (1),
.BR kill (1),
.BR vrwctrl (1)
